			<div class="content" id="post-content-2847209">
									

<p>Big thanks to all these lovely people who read this over in chat!</p>
<ul>
<li>jishwa for wording details</li>
<li>Modern_Erasmus for helpful linguistic rant</li>
<li>Wogglebug for thinking it was fun</li>
<li>Nuke_Fury for phrasing feex</li>
<li>AidenEldritch for being chill</li>
<li>Sirens for liking the containments</li>
</ul>
<p>Image sources:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E8%8A%B1%E5%9C%92%E9%B0%BB.JPG">https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E8%8A%B1%E5%9C%92%E9%B0%BB.JPG</a>
<ul>
<li>Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-Share Alike 3.0 Unported license</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heteroconger_hassi_05.jpg">https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heteroconger_hassi_05.jpg</a>
<ul>
<li>Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-Share Alike 3.0 Unported license</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_Sea_Garden_Eel_-_Gorgasia_sillneri.jpg">https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_Sea_Garden_Eel_-_Gorgasia_sillneri.jpg</a>
<ul>
<li>Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 2.0 Generic license</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Spoilers?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>These eels are pretty old existence-wise, but they like modern dining and vacations. Tryin’ to be hip and stuff.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>It is my headcanon that their moving in and out of the burrows is accompanied by a “nyeeeeoooop” sound effect.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Additional&nbsp;reading:</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Additional&nbsp;reading&nbsp;and&nbsp;other&nbsp;fun&nbsp;stuff:</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>So&#8230; I really like aquariums. And I really like documentaries. And I also really like Sir David Attenborough!</p>
<p>There's a video of Sir David's documentary, &quot;Desert Seas&quot; on YouTube: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cpkG1Vn81oU&amp;t=3s">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cpkG1Vn81oU&amp;t=3s</a> at around the 24:27 mark, you can see garden eels going in and out of their burrows.</p>
<p>People also keep garden eels in personal aquariums! It's pretty hard to feed them though. <a href="http://www.advancedaquarist.com/2011/7/fish2">http://www.advancedaquarist.com/2011/7/fish2</a></p>
<p>Things I referred to while writing:<br />
<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indo-Pacific">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indo-Pacific</a><br />
<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_Life_London_Aquarium">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_Life_London_Aquarium</a><br />
<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aquarium_Berlin">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aquarium_Berlin</a><br />
<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monterey_Bay_Aquarium">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monterey_Bay_Aquarium</a><br />
<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heterocongrinae">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heterocongrinae</a><br />
<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siglos">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siglos</a><br />
<a href="http://www.mypersiancorner.com/2013/06/how-can-i-thank-you-let-me-count-ways.html">http://www.mypersiancorner.com/2013/06/how-can-i-thank-you-let-me-count-ways.html</a><br />
<a href="http://www.wikihow.com/Say-Thank-You-in-Persian">http://www.wikihow.com/Say-Thank-You-in-Persian</a></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

